msgid "RELEASE NOTES FOR LIBGUESTFS 1.52"
msgstr "НОТАТКИ ЩОДО ВИПУСКУ LIBGUESTFS 1.12"

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:7
msgid ""
"These are the release notes for libguestfs stable release 1.52.  This "
"describes the major changes since 1.50."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:10
msgid "Libguestfs 1.52.0 was released on B<5 January 2024>."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:14
msgid ""
"The Python bindings now use C<bytes> (instead of C<str>) for the event "
"callback message, since it may contain arbitrary 8 bit data (thanks Yonatan "
"Shtarkman)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:18
msgid ""
"Also in the Python bindings, fix a rare crash, and avoid memory leaks in "
"event callbacks (thanks Yonatan Shtarkman, Laszlo Ersek, Eric Blake)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:22
msgid ""
"Support for OCaml 5, and OCaml E<ge> 4.07 is now the minimum (thanks "
"Guillaume Munch-Maccagnoni, Jerry James, Josh Berdine, Jürgen Hötzel, "
"Vincent Laviron)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:26
msgid ""
"The OCaml bindings now release the runtime lock around calls to "
"C<guestfs_close>, since that call might be long-running (for example it "
"might have to shut down the appliance and synch disks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:32
msgid "Support OpencloudOS (cunshunxia@tencent)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:36
msgid ""
"SELinux relabelling now runs in parallel, meaning it's a lot quicker (Andrey "
"Drobyshev)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:39
msgid ""
"Add support for lzma and zstd compression methods in tar APIs (like "
"C<guestfs_tar_in>) (Zixun LI)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:42
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_pvs_full> previously didn't always return the correct device "
"names.  This has now been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:45
msgid ""
"C<guestfs_btrfs_filesystem_balance> fixed so it now works with more modern "
"btrfs tools (Jürgen Hötzel)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:50
msgid ""
"The L<guestfish(1)> I<--key> option now recognizes LVM names like F</dev/"
"mapper/rhel_bootp--73--75--123-root> (Laszlo Ersek)."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:53
msgid ""
"guestfish I<--key> option also supports a new S<I<--key all:...>> selector "
"to try the same key on all devices."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:56
msgid ""
"In L<guestmount(1)> avoid calling C<fclose(NULL)> on error paths, which "
"might have caused a crash on some platforms."
msgstr ""

#. type: textblock
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.52.pod:61
msgid ""
"The C<RELEASES> file (which listed release dates) has been removed and "
"replaced with a simple C<RELEASE_DATE> macro in F<./configure>.  This should "
